      "proof_review": {
        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Complete author Theorem1.17 proof in Section4, including its new projection/subspace reduction and correlation identification, is read and supplied. X is countable, K=l2(X) direct-sum l2(X) with the conjugate-swap involution Gamma, P belongs to Gr(K,Gamma), and the finite occupied/empty subsets are disjoint with P K intersect(K_plus occupied direct-sum K_minus empty)={0}. The conditional law on the deleted configuration space is exactly the PfPP corresponding to the orthogonal projection onto (P K plus K_plus occupied plus K_minus empty) intersect the remaining doubled space. The local regularity/decomposition lemmas state the finite reductions explicitly; symmetric routine cases are identified as such by the source. The full existence proof1.3/2.2 is included; prior Araki quasi-free states and the standard finite-dimensional projection reduction are author-cited background. No Schur-perfectness, shifted-Schur or continuous-space extension is separately counted."
      },
